{"seq":20,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-full-a-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T20:48:19.496Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"44235d226f61756c96f98542569eafe2d183c4c7775869b4307fa211b35bc651","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Moss's notes mention two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n1. **#PD-4492**, from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell opened it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers checking in at doors 14–18 of the Eau Claire yard weren't getting their bay assignments by text. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed the 04:00 shift on 5 Oct got through the gate with no manual help.\n2. **#4419**, from \"Moss: North cheat sheet\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was then escalated to tier-2 support for scanner firmware testing. This note has no date, so I can't tell when the ticket was opened.\n\nBefore you add these to the weekly notes:\n- They're written differently (\"PD-4492\" and \"4419\") and are about different problems, so treat them as two separate tickets.\n- I checked every Moss file I could open, all six (four North, two Central). The Central ones mention tickets #4409 and #4412, but those belong to Marrow Fieldworks, not QFL.\n- I left out Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways.\" That's a different company, not one of our customers, and it isn't one of Moss's notes.\n- Moss hasn't posted in any channel you're in, and the #inc-qfl-sev1 incident on 4 Nov 2025 had no ticket number in the channel."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
